<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thermidorian Reaction</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1794">1794</a>–<a href="/years/1795">1795</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as 9 Thermidor, Fall of Robespierre, Coup of 9 Thermidor</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Thermidorian Reaction was the turn in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolution">French Revolution</a> that began on 9 Thermidor Year II (27 July 1794), when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-convention">National Convention</a> arrested <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maximilien-robespierre">Maximilien Robespierre</a> and his allies; they were guillotined the next day and in the days that followed. The Convention then dismantled the machinery of the Terror, closed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacobin-club">Jacobin Club</a> and freed thousands of prisoners, while a 'White Terror' took revenge on former Jacobins in parts of the south. It ended with the Constitution of the Year III, which established the Directory in 1795.</p></div>
